WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.440 --> 00:00:02.830
[MONKEY NOISES]

00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:09.300
Basically that
means, this is me.

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:10.000
This is Jane.

00:00:13.170 --> 00:00:17.130
I left England to go and
study chimpanzees, not just

00:00:17.130 --> 00:00:21.660
any animal but the
one most like us.

00:00:21.660 --> 00:00:24.410
The DNA of humans
and chimpanzees

00:00:24.410 --> 00:00:27.210
differs by only just over 1%.

00:00:27.210 --> 00:00:32.549
They use certain plants as
medicine, leaves as sponges.

00:00:32.549 --> 00:00:36.730
Each individual has his
or her own personality.

00:00:39.470 --> 00:00:43.940
Chimpanzees have the same
kind of emotions as we do.

00:00:43.940 --> 00:00:48.080
When the old female, Flow,
died, the older child

00:00:48.080 --> 00:00:51.080
kept going back to the
body, pulled the dead hand

00:00:51.080 --> 00:00:54.740
towards him, as though
trying to make her groom him.

00:00:54.740 --> 00:00:57.250
I saw him climb a
tree and look down

00:00:57.250 --> 00:01:00.950
this nest where he and
his mother slept together.

00:01:00.950 --> 00:01:03.980
He climbed down, curled
up on the ground,

00:01:03.980 --> 00:01:06.110
and he died of grief.

00:01:06.110 --> 00:01:08.690
People have said,
well, it's only humans

00:01:08.690 --> 00:01:11.340
who have some kind
of spirituality,

00:01:11.340 --> 00:01:12.290
but I don't think so.

00:01:15.560 --> 00:01:18.260
People need to understand
that chimpanzees

00:01:18.260 --> 00:01:22.520
are sentient and sapient
because these chimpanzees had

00:01:22.520 --> 00:01:23.960
given me so much.

00:01:23.960 --> 00:01:28.180
I knew I had to do something
to conserve their environment.

00:01:28.180 --> 00:01:30.990
So I went to Africa
as a scientist.

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:33.280
I left the jungle
as an activist.

00:01:36.480 --> 00:01:39.470
In this master class, I'd
like to share with you all

00:01:39.470 --> 00:01:43.970
of the amazing things that I
discovered about these closest

00:01:43.970 --> 00:01:45.350
relatives of ours.

00:01:45.350 --> 00:01:47.970
I want to talk about
what we all can do

00:01:47.970 --> 00:01:50.600
together to right the wrongs.

00:01:50.600 --> 00:01:52.820
You have an indomitable spirit.

00:01:52.820 --> 00:01:56.030
You can make change
in your own life

00:01:56.030 --> 00:01:59.720
every single day to make
this a better world.

00:01:59.720 --> 00:02:02.070
There is still a window of time.

00:02:02.070 --> 00:02:06.142
Nature can win, if
we give her a chance.

00:02:06.142 --> 00:02:10.080
I'm Jane Goodall, and
this is my master class.

